# AI assistant working notes (local only, never published).
# Bare `CLAUDE.md` at the root is the intended one; the `**/` pattern is because
# a `mirobody/pulse/CLAUDE.md` was committed once and shipped to PyPI inside the
# wheel — an internal notes file, under a filename that tells open-source
# readers to skip it. Its content was real module documentation and now lives at
# mirobody/pulse/README.md.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Internal testing results — LOCAL ONLY, deliberately.
#
# Our own measurements are not what an open-source reader needs. What they need
# is a demo they can run (`examples/`) and a claim they can check themselves
# (`pytest mirobody/test_engine_coverage.py -s` prints the published score). The
# rule for which side a number falls on: backed by a test in the repo that
# anyone can run -> publishable; produced by `eval/` -> not.
docs/internal-testing.md

# Resolver evaluation harness — LOCAL ONLY, deliberately.
#
# `eval/` holds the maintained test set, the runner, and every timestamped
# result. It stays out of the repo for two reasons and neither is tidiness:
# the test set is derived in part from a sibling private repo's curated seed,
# and a published benchmark that ships alongside the thing it grades is an
# invitation to tune against it. Kept on disk so a change to the resolver can
# be re-scored against the same set and the same runner — reproducible,
# upgradable, traceable — without becoming a public claim.
eval/
